Name the ZALLOC/LAST entry that does not return, by dispatching

zone_tagging_on defaults to false ("-zt"), so all 644 __zone_site_register calls
are no-ops and the stall cannot be inside them.  The other 56 entries in that
slot (smr domains, btlog, kheap/zone-view startup, vm_paging_map) printed
nothing, which is why the last Z line and the stall never coincided.

Print func and arg from the dispatcher for every entry in that slot.  The print
sits above the call, so the last line on the panel is the entry that never
returned, whatever function it is.  This sits after nio-startup-tokens so both
insertions land at the same anchor without fighting over it.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -420,5 +420,10 @@ kernel_startup_initialize_upto(startup_subsystem_id_t upto)
 				printf("\n[#%u:%u.%u]", nio_this, cur->subsystem,
 				    (unsigned)(cur->rank % 100u));
 			}
 		}
+		if (cur->subsystem == STARTUP_SUB_ZALLOC &&
+		    cur->rank == STARTUP_RANK_LAST) {
+			printf("\nF%x.%x", (unsigned)((uintptr_t)cur->func & 0xffffffu),
+			    (unsigned)((uintptr_t)cur->arg & 0xffffffu));
+		}
 		cur->func(cur->arg);
